ADP security rebuilds of upstream tools, 2026-09-27.
Exact source commits and reviewed dependency patches: source-lock.json.

Buildx 0.37.1 (Apache-2.0), Helm 3.22.0 (Apache-2.0),
runc 1.4.3 (Apache-2.0), osscontainertools/docker-credential-acr (Apache-2.0).
Go toolchain 1.26.8. The build retains upstream tool behavior and upgrades
vulnerable Go modules. Upstream license texts are copied into the final image.

Docker daemon 29.8.1 and containerd 2.4.1 come from checksum-pinned upstream
release archives. AWS CLI 2.37.4 is rebuilt from its pinned upstream source with
Python 3.14.7; its license and third-party licenses accompany the executable.

Node20 paths are compatibility links to supported Node24 runtimes. This is an
intentional runtime migration, not a Node20 security backport.
The original licenses for all embedded Go dependencies remain available from
their checksum-verified module sources. Complete module metadata is embedded
in the rebuilt binaries and recorded by the candidate SBOM.
